],"id":"euler.lemma-5.7","kind":"claim","label":"Lemma 5.7","locator":"Lemma 5.7, Section 5","source_id":"paper","statement":"**Lemma 5.7.** Let $g_0(t,a,s)$ be smooth and independent of the phase at the labels outside $\\operatorname{supp}g$. Assume its phase average extends smoothly and periodically in $a$ across the cell faces. There is an absolute exponent $C$ such that, for every integer $m\\ge0$ and every $t\\in[t_0,T]$, $$\\begin{align}\n \\sum_{|\\beta|=m}\\|\\partial_x^\\beta g_0^\\natural(t)\\|_{L^\\infty}\n &\\le C_m(\\mathsf D^C\\lambda^{3/2})^m\\gamma(t)\n                  \\|g_0\\|_{[m],\\gamma}, \\tag{5.44}\\\\\n \\|g_0^\\natural(t)\\|_{C^{m,1/2}}\n &\\le C_m(\\mathsf D^C\\lambda^{3/2})^{m+1}\\gamma(t)\n                  \\|g_0\\|_{[m+1],\\gamma}. \\tag{5.45}\n\\end{align}$$ Both bounds also hold on $[0,T]$ with $\\gamma$ replaced by one, and for a phase-independent field with $\\mathsf D^C\\lambda^{3/2}$ replaced by $\\mathsf D^C$.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/nodes/euler.lemma-5.7","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/nodes/euler.lemma-5.7","id":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/edges/%5B%22euler.lemma-5.7%22%2C%22euler.lemma-d.1%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/edges/%5B%22euler.lemma-5.7%22%2C%22euler.lemma-d.1%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/nodes/euler.lemma-d.1"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/nodes/euler.lemma-5.7","id":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/edges/%5B%22euler.lemma-5.7%22%2C%22euler.proposition-5.1%2